        + Beta 5.1.13:
          - Flexible Colon Requirements for if/while Statements:
            - Inline Syntax (Same line): Colon (:) is STRICTLY REQUIRED when the conditional statement and its body are on the same line.
              - Valid: `if x > 5: say "hi"`
              - Invalid: `if x > 5 say "hi"` → Raises [S005] "Expected ':' after block header in inline statement"
            - Multi-line Syntax (Different lines): Colon (:) is OPTIONAL when the body is on subsequent lines.
              - Valid: `if x > 5\n    say "hi"` (no colon)
              - Valid: `if x > 5:\n    say "hi"` (with colon)
            - Implementation:
              - Updated parse_control_statement() in main/pars/stmt.py to detect inline vs multi-line cases.
              - For if statements: Check for colon and split condition from inline body. If inline body exists, parse as single statement. If no colon, check for statement keywords after condition to detect missing colon error (S005).
              - For while statements: Same logic as if statements.
              - For elif statements: Applied same inline/multi-line detection logic.
              - Error handling: Raise BicalaSyntaxError with code S005 when inline content is detected without colon.
            - Lợi ích:
              - Flexible: Supports both inline and multi-line syntaxes for better code readability.
              - Consistent: Applies same rules to if, while, and elif statements.
              - Error detection: Provides clear error message (S005) when colon is missing in inline statements.
